@startuml control-flow-diagram-payment-validation
title Payment Validation Sub-Process (8 nodes - under 10 limit)

' This is a SUB-DIAGRAM referenced from the main Order Processing workflow
' Demonstrates how to keep complex sub-processes under the 10-node business limit

skinparam activityBackgroundColor #FFFACD
skinparam activityBorderColor #A80036

|Order Processing System|
start
note right
  **SUB-DIAGRAM**
  Called from: control-flow-diagram-order-processing.puml
  Entry Point: Execute Payment Validation
end note

:Validate Payment Method;
note right
  Node count: 1 (process step)
  Check if credit card or PayPal
end note

if (Payment Method Valid?) then (yes)
  note right
    Node count: 2 (decision point)
  end note

  :Contact Payment Gateway;
  note right
    Node count: 3 (process step)
    External System: Stripe/PayPal API
  end note

  if (Gateway Reachable?) then (yes)
    note right
      Node count: 4 (decision point)
    end note

    :Authorize Payment;
    note right
      Node count: 5 (process step)
      Verify funds/credit available
    end note

    if (Payment Authorized?) then (yes)
      note right
        Node count: 6 (decision point)
      end note

      :Update Payment Status to "APPROVED";
      note right
        Node count: 7 (process step)
      end note

      stop
      note right
        Node count: 8 (end - success path)
        **Return to main diagram with success status**
      end note

    else (no)
      :Update Payment Status to "DECLINED";
      note left
        Insufficient funds or card declined
      end note
      stop
      note left
        **Return to main diagram with failure status**
      end note
    endif

  else (no)
    :Update Payment Status to "GATEWAY_ERROR";
    note left
      Payment gateway timeout or unavailable
    end note
    stop
    note left
      **Return to main diagram with error status**
    end note
  endif

else (no)
  :Update Payment Status to "INVALID_METHOD";
  note left
    Unsupported payment method
  end note
  stop
  note left
    **Return to main diagram with failure status**
  end note
endif

legend right
  **SUB-DIAGRAM NODE COUNT**: 8 nodes (under 15-node limit - compliant ✓)

  **Node Breakdown**:
  - Start: 1 node (implied)
  - Process steps: 4 nodes (Validate Method, Contact Gateway, Authorize Payment, Update Status)
  - Decision points: 3 nodes (Method Valid?, Gateway Reachable?, Payment Authorized?)
  - End: 1 node (primary success path)

  **Returns to Main Diagram**: control-flow-diagram-order-processing.puml
  **Return Values**: APPROVED, DECLINED, GATEWAY_ERROR, INVALID_METHOD

  **Source Traceability**:
  - Phase 4 BP-ORDER-001 Step 2 (Payment Validation)
  - Phase 3 ORDER-BR-010 (Payment Authorization Rule)
  - Phase 3 ORDER-BR-011 (Payment Gateway Integration Rule)
endlegend

@enduml
